   "design": "Treatment rooms use two-bin shelves with barcodes: when a bin is empty its label is scanned, and the purchasing system ({PROCUREMENT}) builds the order from a standing list of contracted items and prices, so stock is not counted and items are not looked up. The physician assistant checks the order, and once checked it goes to purchasing in the system. Deliveries are scanned against the order. Choosing new equipment stays with the physician assistant.",
   "previous_blocker": "Stock was counted by eye and orders typed from the catalogue.",
   "enabler_now": "Two-bin scanning and standing order lists run in hospital purchasing systems.",
   "still_hard": "Special items are not on the standing list.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing which supply the next clinic day will run short of.",
